ECDSA digital signatures (secp256k1): the guest signs every booking with a private key and the network checks it with the public key, so nobody can fake a booking or a payment.

Keccak-256 hashing: each block stores the hash of the previous block, so the bookings form a linked chain.

Smart contract security was further enhanced through 
the use of Solidity’s require() statements. These validation checks prevent unauthorized actions, ensure correct payment amounts and verify room availability
before processing transactions. This reduces the likelihood of invalid or malicious transactions being executed on the blockchain.

